# Pairs with TypeOK. A key's prepare is appended again and again, which a
# bounded WAL does not admit. (Production keys a re-staged prepare by its
# AtomicBatchIndex, so a retried prepare never completes a batch twice.)
MODULE: TypeOkPrepareRepeated
TARGET: TypeOK
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a key is prepared without bound
PERTURBS: Prepare

--- FIND
    /\ x \notin Prepared
    /\ wal' = [wal EXCEPT ![KeyPart[x]] = Append(@, [k |-> "prep", x |-> x])]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: a key may be prepared again.
    /\ TRUE
    /\ wal' = [wal EXCEPT ![KeyPart[x]] = Append(@, [k |-> "prep", x |-> x])]
--- END
